WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.648
The install runs on Node and pnpm: the backend builds, the suites pass, and the full verification harness reports seven of seven green. OneShot is ready to run.

2
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:26.014
The Verified Agentic Console loads ready with offline dry-run enabled, so no API key is needed. A five-step onboarding starts at Understand: read the fixture, then run it.

3
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:39.243
Step two offers four pre-loaded scenarios; the four-partition sandbox is selected. The prompt shows each partition tag, and one click tries it.

4
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:56.967
The button turns to executing and the pipeline reads stream in progress. Four live columns appear, and the Python runtime runs as a subprocess by default, with optional HTTP RPC.

5
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:11.637
The stream completes as fixture verified, and the result card records a successful HTTP response with the SHA-256 hash confirmed byte for byte. Every column settles to verified.

6
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:24.408
Open the context drawer and the context tab shows the stored source and the session restore fields: every run keeps its original input, ready to restore into a new session.

7
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:44.968
The backends tab enforces virtual mode and blocks path traversal. Four partitions: workspace durable, scratch ephemeral, memories across sessions, and artifacts immutable. How secure a deployment is still depends on configuration.

8
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:55.252
The governance panel shows two review checkpoints: the first waits for approval with a confirm button, the second waits for a verified package hash. Neither advances on its own.

9
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:11.117
Live provider configuration lets you switch between Gemini, Openai, and Nebius. Only the config source changes; the same workflow and the same event stream contract run against the real provider.

10
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:28.139
Expand the reasoning chain: the goal, the execution phase, and the invariant results emitted by the local Python subprocess. A verified badge confirms the SHA-256 contract matched byte for byte.

11
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:40.974
Tool execution runs against workspace files and emits real output records. The event log lists pipeline stages with timestamps, no synthetic delays, no mocked results.

12
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:58.617
Offline fixture verification and live agentic execution follow the same verifiable contract: real streams, real hash proofs, real partition isolation. Clone the repository, install, and run the launcher.
